   "description": "The observer presses SPACE on a dark field with a dim cross; [[param:start_delay]] later the lit card is exposed for [[param:exposure]]. A cue then names one row: in the paper a high, middle or low tone; here a bar beside that row for [[param:cue_duration]] ([[param:cue_mode]] cue). Its onset is set per block from the card's offset ([[param:cue_delays_s]]). The observer types the cued row into boxes and presses Enter; a symbol counts only in its correct position. Delay blocks run in ascending and descending series ([[param:n_series]]), each opened by sample trials.",
   "sourceFiles": [
    "src/sperling1960/task.py",
    "src/sperling1960/phases.py",
    "src/sperling1960/stimuli.py",
    "src/sperling1960/materials.py",
    "configs/task.yaml"
   ],
   "notes": [
    "One task runs all four parameter sets: task.yaml (4/4/4 L&N, Experiment 4), task-9.yaml (3/3/3), task-exp3.yaml (all four materials at 0 s) and task-whole.yaml (Experiment 1 whole report: no cue phases, every symbol typed). The timeline and drawing show task.yaml.",
    "Paper values: 50 ms exposure, 0.5 s start delay, tones 2500/650/250 cps about 0.5 s, cue delays −0.10 to 1.0 s, card 5 × 8 in at 22 in, capitals about 0.45 in.",
    "Deviation: the tone is replaced by a visual bar (alhazen 2.16.0 has no event-bound tone); C, H, P, R are removed from the letters (experimenter keys); typed boxes replace a written response grid.",
    "ASSUMED (not in the paper): letter and row spacing, the bar's size and position, response boxes, the 60 s caps on starting and reporting, and 6 test trials per delay block.",
    "No inter-trial interval is drawn: iti is 0 ms (paper: the observer set his own rate), so the next trial begins with the Ready phase."
   ]
